@OrderApi_HostAddress = http://localhost:5102

### Run the requests from top to bottom. Later requests use ids from earlier responses.
### There is no login yet. The X-Demo-User header picks the user: alice (the default), bob or admin.
### Prices, stock and payment come from fakes:
###   the price of a book is made from its id (between 5.95 and 44.95 euro),
###   a line of more than 50 copies is out of stock,
###   a total above 500 euro is declined.

### PlaceOrderRequest => Created (alice orders 2 copies of a book)
# @name placed
POST {{OrderApi_HostAddress}}/orders HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [
    { "bookId": "6f1c0a7e-5c0e-4a53-9d4b-1d3a3b8d0001", "quantity": 2 },
    { "bookId": "6f1c0a7e-5c0e-4a53-9d4b-1d3a3b8d0002", "quantity": 1 }
  ]
}

### OrderGetListRequest => OK (alice sees her own orders, newest first)
GET {{OrderApi_HostAddress}}/orders

### OrderGetRequest => OK (the order that was just placed)
GET {{OrderApi_HostAddress}}/orders/{{placed.response.body.$.id}}

### OrderGetRequest => Not Found, because the order belongs to alice (CAT-GEN-1002)
GET {{OrderApi_HostAddress}}/orders/{{placed.response.body.$.id}}
X-Demo-User: bob

### OrderGetListRequest => OK (bob has no orders yet)
GET {{OrderApi_HostAddress}}/orders
X-Demo-User: bob

### OrderGetRequest => OK (an admin sees every order)
GET {{OrderApi_HostAddress}}/orders/{{placed.response.body.$.id}}
X-Demo-User: admin

### PlaceOrderRequest => Bad request, out of stock (CAT-ORD-1002). The order is saved with status Cancelled.
POST {{OrderApi_HostAddress}}/orders HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [
    { "bookId": "6f1c0a7e-5c0e-4a53-9d4b-1d3a3b8d0003", "quantity": 51 }
  ]
}

### PlaceOrderRequest => Bad request, the payment is declined (CAT-ORD-1003). The order is saved with status Cancelled.
### 100 copies cost at least 595 euro, whatever the books cost, which is above the 500 euro limit of the fake.
POST {{OrderApi_HostAddress}}/orders HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [
    { "bookId": "6f1c0a7e-5c0e-4a53-9d4b-1d3a3b8d0004", "quantity": 50 },
    { "bookId": "6f1c0a7e-5c0e-4a53-9d4b-1d3a3b8d0005", "quantity": 50 }
  ]
}

### PlaceOrderRequest => Bad request, no lines
POST {{OrderApi_HostAddress}}/orders HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": []
}

### PlaceOrderRequest => Bad request, several rules fail (book id and quantity)
POST {{OrderApi_HostAddress}}/orders HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [
    { "bookId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000", "quantity": 0 },
    { "bookId": "6f1c0a7e-5c0e-4a53-9d4b-1d3a3b8d0001", "quantity": 100 }
  ]
}

### CancelOrderRequest => No Content (alice cancels her order)
POST {{OrderApi_HostAddress}}/orders/{{placed.response.body.$.id}}/cancel

### CancelOrderRequest => Conflict, the order is already cancelled (CAT-ORD-1004)
POST {{OrderApi_HostAddress}}/orders/{{placed.response.body.$.id}}/cancel

### CancelOrderRequest => Not Found, bob cannot cancel the order of alice
POST {{OrderApi_HostAddress}}/orders/{{placed.response.body.$.id}}/cancel
X-Demo-User: bob

### CleanUpOrderCountersRequest => No Content
### Development only. It simulates the nightly run of the scheduler.
### Deletes the counters of earlier days and creates the counter of today.
POST {{OrderApi_HostAddress}}/development/scheduler/clean-up-order-counters
